<h1>Jennifer Davis</h1>
<p>US House, 8th District, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Republican.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.votejenniferdavis.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (votejenniferdavis.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Davis&#39;s campaign site lists small business, education, immigration, national security, community safety and tax relief as her issues, and says she wants to cut taxes, streamline regulations and expand school options including public, charter, private and home schools. She says she supports securing the border with technology, enforcing existing immigration law and prioritizing legal immigration, and proposes a national cyber defense she calls a Digital Dome. In her Sun-Times questionnaire she names affordability as the district&#39;s most important issue and says she backs term limits and independent redistricting commissions.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Co-founded the field service software company Davisware with her husband and later founded BExponential, an organization for women entrepreneurs; she has not held elected office.</p>
